From: Peter Oberparleiter <oberpar@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gcov: add support for GCC 15

Using gcov on kernels compiled with GCC 15 results in truncated 16-byte
long .gcda files with no usable data.  To fix this, update GCOV_COUNTERS
to match the value defined by GCC 15.

Reported-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
Closes: https://github.com/linux-test-project/lcov/issues/445
Signed-off-by: Peter Oberparleiter <oberpar@linux.ibm.com>
[ Note: This patch has been suggested by Peter, but not sent as it. I
  created this just so this patch can be automatically removed from this
  tree when it will be applied upstream. ]
Signed-off-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
